<h1>Week 27</h1>

<p><strong>From:</strong> Kayla</p>
<p><strong>Artist:</strong> Bright Eyes</p>
<p><strong>Album:</strong> <em>Digital Ash in a Digital Urn</em></p>

<p>Lana,</p>

<p>
My pick for you this week is <em>Digital Ash in a Digital Urn</em> by Bright Eyes. Conor released this album at the same time as <em>I’m Wide Awake, It’s Morning</em>.
</p>

<p>
This album has some of my favorite Bright Eyes songs of all time. I listened to this a lot when you had Bolt in the office building with the loft, so I always remember cleaning a lot of screens and listening to this lol.
</p>

<p>
Favorite songs:
</p>

<ul>
<li>Gold Mine Gutted</li>
<li>Take It Easy (Love Nothing)</li>
<li>Hit the Switch</li>
<li>Devil in the Details</li>
<li>Ship in a Bottle</li>
<li>Theme to Piñata</li>
<li>Easy/Lucky/Free</li>
<li>I Believe in Symmetry</li>
</ul>

<p>
“Gold Mine Gutted” is probably one of my favorites ever. It makes me think about my twenties, and it also makes me think about you in your twenties. I do not know why, but that song reminds me of you.
</p>

<p>
“Take It Easy (Love Nothing),” “Hit the Switch,” and “Devil in the Details” are probably in my top 10 Bright Eyes songs of all time. They both just have so much meaning to me.
</p>

<p>
In “Hit the Switch,” the second verse where he talks about his friend out west always makes me think of Kiera.
</p>

<p>
“Ship in a Bottle” is also amazing, and I laugh my butt off every time when the baby cries. Anytime you talk to Tamar about this album, she always says, “I love Ship in a Bottle… except that baby part… that scares me.” Omg, without fail she says it every time 😂😂😂
</p>

<p>
I really like “Theme to Piñata,” “Easy/Lucky/Free,” and “I Believe in Symmetry” too.
</p>

<p>
Kayla
</p>

